# Chroma library, modern Earth: the learning sphere's events as they touch a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3). Design: chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-data/learn.json (events with on_character and the modern epoch; each scene is built on the
# event's wording.modern and on_character). Face words: chroma-library/earth_spheres.py. Fields: build.py (the spheres'
# fields of world-fields.md, 2026-10-09).
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event the Engine fires on its sphere event (sphere_event: <key>) for the
# people its selector names (place, members or all); per_year is all 0 and there are no drivers. The '# world:' line
# above each moment gives the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who meet the moment (estimate).
# Sixteen moments, one per learn event of the modern epoch that has on_character. Tone follows the event's tone (good =
# joy, bad = trouble, mixed = mixed): 6 joy, 6 trouble, 4 mixed.
#
# Near neighbours in earth.py, kept apart on purpose: the_exam is the ranking number and what to do with it (earth.py
# has the revision, the last exam and the pass); newcomer_taught is the neighbours' side, the family in the flat below
# ('a new kid joins your class' and 'learning the local language' hold the pupil's and the newcomer's sides);
# learned_leave is the graduating class leaving together ('work and a room abroad' is one cousin's offer);
# teachers_walk_out is the parents' six weeks ('a strike vote at work' holds a worker's own vote).
#
# Children and schools: pupils from 12 appear in the school moments (two more years, the number, books pulled, the
# library, the weekend school, the closed schools, the flat below). Every option a pupil can pick is safe: no truancy,
# no danger, no harm to any child, and the war stays off-page (the fighting is never shown).
#
# Options: sphere: on each is the face the act is in (one-colour X: learn.X; a pair: its pair face in wheel order, so
# WR is learn.RW, WG learn.GW, UG learn.GU). Levers (lever:) where the act plainly is one, from character.levers.
#
# Layout: each a life event with the five one-colour options and one pair set. The 16 use all twelve halves of D1 to D6,
# four of them twice (D1a, D3a, D5b, D6b), each chosen to hold the event's own pair faces where it has them.
# Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so every
# colour has the same mean chance in each moment and in every stage. No flags.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge_lost (pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event knowledge_lost, selector place, share .3
== nobody can find the drawings for the pumps
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: knowledge_lost
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: knowledge_lost (sphere learn). Selector place: a skill held by one or two people goes when its keeper retires or dies, and then something fails that only they understood; about 3 in 10 of the people living there are touched by the failure enough to act on it (share .3, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: an old town with old works, a skill never written down, a family that worked on it
rarer: a new town, a person who never deals with the works or the council
tone: trouble
life: community, work, home
horizon: months
roles: elder, grandparent, colleague
earth: the engineer who understood the town's old water system has retired, and when it fails nobody can find the drawings
scene: The engineer who understood the town's old water system has retired to the coast. This week the pumps failed, half of {place} has no water, and nobody at the council can find the drawings.
scene W: The council says it is working on it. {N} thinks of the old neighbours carrying water up the stairs, and of how this was allowed to happen.
scene U: Somewhere there must be a record of how the pipes run. {N} wants to find it, or else work it out.
scene B: Whoever understands the old system now can name their price. {N} sees that plainly.
scene R: {N} has never been inside the pumping station, and would very much like to get a look at those pumps.
scene G: {grandparent} helped lay those pipes as a young man, and used to talk about where they ran.
- W | press the council to have the whole system written down, with copies kept for all | v: universalism, security | lever: voice | pushes: institution council | sphere: learn.W | chance: 68
- U | ring the retired engineer and ask him to talk you through the system | act: ring the retired engineer and ask him to talk them through the system | v: self-direction | sphere: learn.U | chance: 61
- B | learn the old system first, and offer the council your help at a price | act: learn the old system first, and offer the council their help at a price | v: achievement, power | sphere: learn.B | chance: 68
- R | go down with the repair crew and learn the pumps by trying them | v: stimulation | mark: learned a skill | sphere: learn.R | chance: 74
- G | walk the route of the pipes with the old men who laid them | v: tradition | sphere: learn.G | chance: 58
- BG | study each burst pipe as it is dug up, and write down what it teaches | v: security, universalism | sphere: learn.BG | chance: 62
- BR | teach yourself the pumps from manuals at night, and mend one on your own | act: teach themselves the pumps from manuals at night, and mend one on their own | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: learn.BR | chance: 44
- UG | record what the old pipe-layers remember before it is lost as well | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: learn.GU | chance: 64
- WR | start a class for the young plumbers, so no skill rests with one person again | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: learn.RW | chance: 50
- WU | draw up a plain manual of the whole system for whoever comes next | v: universalism, security | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 56
works: The drawings turn up in a box at the old works, and {N} helps put the water back on.
works: This time the system is written down, and {Ns} name is in the notes.
fails: The water comes back after three weeks, and still nobody knows how the system works.
fails: The repair holds for a year, then the pumps fail again, and the town is back where it started.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- first_school (pairs D4b)

# world: sphere event first_school, selector place, share .3
== a new school across the river
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: first_school
who: teacher
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 24-55
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: first_school (sphere learn). Selector place: a school opens where the children had to travel out; about 3 in 10 of the people living there have a child of school age who could go and face the choice (share .3, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it (estimate)
likelier: a growing quarter or a far bank with no school, a young family, a long bus ride to the old school
rarer: no children of school age, a town with schools in every quarter
tone: joy
life: family, children, community
horizon: years
roles: child, parent, mentor, teacher
earth: a new school opens across the river, and your child no longer takes the early bus out of town
scene: A new school has opened across the river, so {child} no longer has to take the early bus out of town. The new head stands at the gate every morning, and the old school in town has places to spare.
scene W: The head says every child on the far bank will have a place. {N} would like to see that it is true.
scene U: {N} wants to sit in on a lesson and meet the teachers before deciding anything.
scene B: A new school is still deciding who sits on its board and how it is run. {N} sees a chance to have a say.
scene R: Ten minutes' walk instead of an hour on the bus. {N} pictures {child} with the whole morning back.
scene G: {child}'s cousins all go to the old school in town, and the family has gone there for three generations.
- W | go door to door on the far bank, so every family knows a place is theirs | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: learn.W | chance: 79
- U | sit in on a lesson, and ask the new teacher how they teach reading | v: self-direction | sphere: learn.U | chance: 72
- B | stand for the new school's board in its first year | v: power, achievement | lever: lead | pushes: institution school | sphere: learn.B | chance: 62
- R | move your child to the new school in the first week, and see how it goes | act: move their child to the new school in the first week, and see how it goes | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: exit | pushes: institution school | sphere: learn.R | chance: 72
- G | keep your child at the old school in town, with the cousins | act: keep their child at the old school in town, with the cousins | v: tradition, security | lever: loyalty | pushes: institution school | sphere: learn.G | chance: 74
- BR | spend the free morning hour reading together, whatever book the child picks | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: learn.BR | chance: 80
- UB | read the new school's reports and the teachers' records before you choose | act: read the new school's reports and the teachers' records before they choose | v: achievement, security | sphere: learn.UB | chance: 70
- UG | help the class start a garden by the river and record what grows | v: universalism, tradition | sphere: learn.GU | chance: 60
- WG | join the parents' committee that helps build and keep the new school | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: learn.GW | chance: 66
- WR | speak up at the meeting for the far bank's children to get the first places | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: institution school | sphere: learn.RW | chance: 50
works: {child} settles in by the first winter, and the new teacher becomes a name at the dinner table.
works: The school becomes the heart of the far bank, and {N} knows half the parents by name.
fails: The new school is short of teachers in its second year, and the classes double in size.
fails: {child} misses the old friends from the bus, and the first term is a hard one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- academy_founded (pairs D2b)

# world: sphere event academy_founded, selector place, share .5
== a university on the old army base
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: academy_founded
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-60
times: World event: academy_founded (sphere learn). Selector place: a university or college opens in a town that had none; about half of the people living there feel it in their own life, a course, a job, a rent or a changed street (share .5, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it at all (estimate)
likelier: a mid-sized town with land to spare, a young person who wanted to study, a home near the new campus
rarer: a remote village, a person settled in work far from the campus
tone: joy
life: community, school, work
horizon: years
roles: friend, grandparent, child
earth: a university campus opens on the old army base: rents rise, cafes open, and the town fills with the young
scene: A university campus has opened on the old army base. Rents are rising, cafes have opened on every corner, and {place} is suddenly full of the young. There is a notice by the gate for evening courses.
scene W: The university has promised to take a share of its students from {place}. {N} wants to see the town's own young get in.
scene U: Lectures, a library, people who argue for a living. {N} has wanted something like this for years.
scene B: The university is the biggest employer in town now, and every job there comes with a free course. {N} has noticed.
scene R: The town has woken up. {N} wants to be at every open lecture and every late debate in the new cafes.
scene G: {Ns} family has lived in {place} for generations, and the old neighbours are being priced out of the street.
- W | help the town school's leavers fill in their university applications | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: learn.W | chance: 85
- U | sign up for the evening course you have always meant to take | act: sign up for the evening course they have always meant to take | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: learn.U | chance: 67
- B | take a job in the university office, for the free course that comes with it | v: achievement | sphere: learn.B | chance: 74
- R | talk your way into the labs' open day and try every machine they let you touch | act: talk their way into the labs' open day and try every machine they are let touch | v: stimulation | sphere: learn.R | chance: 80
- G | lead the new students on a walk of the town's old streets and stories | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
- RG | coach the students' new walking club in the hills you know by heart | act: coach the students' new walking club in the hills they know by heart | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: learn.RG | chance: 66
- UB | find out which departments will hire locals, before the posts are advertised | v: achievement, power | sphere: learn.UB | chance: 62
- UG | help the university count and map the wildlife living on the old base | v: universalism | sphere: learn.GU | chance: 70
- WB | start a small scholarship for one local child each year, in the family's name | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | pushes: institution university | sphere: learn.WB | chance: 56
- WR | campaign for free places for the town's poorer children, and fill the hall to do it | v: universalism | lever: voice | pushes: institution university | sphere: learn.RW | chance: 40
works: Within a year {N} has a foot in the new world up on the hill, and new friends from it.
works: The town changes, and {N} changes with it, mostly for the better.
fails: The rents keep climbing, and the old neighbours leave the street one by one.
fails: The campus stays a world apart behind its fence, and {N} never quite finds a way in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- schools_for_all (pairs D3a)

# world: sphere event schools_for_all, selector all, share .8
== two more years at school
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: schools_for_all
stages: juvenile
age: 14-17
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 1-3
times: World event: schools_for_all (sphere learn). Selector all: the leaving age rises by two years; about 8 in 10 of the pupils who were about to leave feel it as a turn in their own plans (share .8, estimate), once in a life, and only for those of that age when it passes (estimate)
likelier: a pupil who meant to leave for work, a family business, a trade school nearby
rarer: a pupil who meant to stay on anyway
tone: mixed
life: school, family, work
horizon: years
roles: parent, friend, mentor
earth: the leaving age rises by two years, and you stay at school instead of starting work this summer
scene: The leaving age has gone up by two years, so {N} will not leave school this summer after all. The older pupils grumble in the corridors, the trade school's lists are full, and {parent} had been counting on help in the family shop.
scene W: A rule for everyone is fair, {N} supposes. Two more years is two more years to learn.
scene U: Two more years means subjects {N} never had time for. Some of them might turn out to be interesting.
scene B: Now everyone stays to eighteen, so a certificate alone will not stand out. {N} wants the one that does.
scene R: {N} was ready to start at the garage this summer. Now it is two more years at a desk.
scene G: {parent} needs the help in the shop now, not in two years, and {N} knows it.
- W | stay on and keep up every subject, the way the new rule intends | v: conformity | sphere: learn.W | chance: 70
- U | pick the hardest subject on offer, just to see what it is like | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: learn.U | chance: 62
- B | choose the subjects that lead to the best-paid courses, and work for top marks | v: achievement | sphere: learn.B | chance: 65
- R | spend two afternoons a week in the trade school's workshop, tools in hand | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: learn.R | chance: 74
- G | help in the family shop after school and on Saturdays | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: learn.G | chance: 68
- BG | ask last year's leavers what they wish they had done, and do that | v: security | sphere: learn.BG | chance: 66
- RG | join the school's outdoor club, and learn the hills and the river by feel | v: stimulation | sphere: learn.RG | chance: 64
- UB | read the new rules closely, and find the course that counts toward a trade licence | v: achievement, security | sphere: learn.UB | chance: 70
- WR | speak up at the school council for trade classes for everyone who wants them | v: universalism | lever: voice | pushes: institution school | sphere: learn.RW | chance: 54
- WU | ask the teachers to set out what the two years must cover, and keep to it | v: security, conformity | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 72
works: The two extra years open a door {N} did not know was there.
works: {N} leaves at eighteen with a certificate and a plan, and {parent} is proud.
fails: {N} counts the days for two years and leaves with little to show for them.
fails: The family shop struggles without the extra hands, and {N} feels the weight of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the_exam (pairs D5b)

# world: sphere event the_exam, selector members, share .8
== four points short on the results letter
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: the_exam
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 16-25
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 1-5
times: World event: the_exam (sphere learn). Selector members: the year's candidates for an entrance exam that ranks them by one number; about 8 in 10 of those who sit it get a number that leaves a real choice to make (share .8, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: places that go by one ranked exam, a first choice with few places, a family that paid for tutors
rarer: a road into work that needs no exam
tone: mixed
life: school, family
horizon: years
roles: parent, grandparent, mentor, friend
earth: after a week of entrance exams and a summer of waiting, a number decides which doors are open, and yours is a few points short
scene: After a week of entrance exams and a summer of waiting, the letter has come with one number on it. It is four points short of the course {N} wanted, and just enough for the second choice.
scene W: The test was the same for everyone. {N} sat it, and the number is the number.
scene U: {N} is sure that two answers were marked wrong, and wants to see the paper.
scene B: Four points. {N} knows people who got in with less, by other doors.
scene R: A whole summer waiting on one number. {N} would rather go and do something than sit another year of tests.
scene G: The college near home is a short bus ride away, and {grandparent} would like {N} close.
- W | accept the second choice, and give it your best from the first day | act: accept the second choice, and give it their best from the first day | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: learn.W | chance: 71
- U | ask to see the marked paper, and learn exactly where the four points went | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: learn.U | chance: 65
- B | take the second choice, and start planning a transfer in the first week | v: achievement, power | sphere: learn.B | chance: 64
- R | turn the place down, and work with your hands for a year before deciding | act: turn the place down, and work with their hands for a year before deciding | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: turned down a chance | lever: exit | sphere: learn.R | chance: 56
- G | take the place at the college near home, close to the family | v: tradition, security | mark: stayed home | sphere: learn.G | chance: 60
- BR | teach yourself the first year's course over the summer, your own way | act: teach themselves the first year's course over the summer, their own way | v: self-direction | sphere: learn.BR | chance: 64
- RG | spend the summer working at the outdoor centre, and decide in the autumn | v: stimulation, hedonism | sphere: learn.RG | chance: 60
- UG | ask the old teacher who knows you best which road truly suits you | act: ask the old teacher who knows them best which road truly suits them | v: self-direction, tradition | sphere: learn.GU | chance: 56
- WB | apply for the scholarship place that asks two years of service in return | v: achievement, security | sphere: learn.WB | chance: 44
- WU | sit the exam again next year, with a plan for every paper | v: achievement, conformity | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 50
works: {N} ends up somewhere that suits {N} better than the first choice would have.
works: A year on, the number no longer matters much, and {N} knows it.
fails: The second choice never feels like {Ns} own, and {N} drifts through it.
fails: The second try or the transfer goes nowhere, and {N} loses a year.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- discovery (pairs D4a)

# world: sphere event discovery, selector place, share .3
== the works is hiring two hundred
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: discovery
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-64
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: discovery (sphere learn). Selector place: a finding at a nearby university or lab is made into work in the town; about 3 in 10 of the working-age people living there feel it in their own work or plans (share .3, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: a town near a university, an old works standing empty, a person looking for work or a new trade
rarer: a person settled in a job they love, a remote village
tone: joy
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: friend, colleague, parent
earth: a lab at the regional university finds a cheaper way to store power, and the local works hires two hundred people
scene: A lab at the regional university has found a cheaper way to store power, and the old works on the edge of {place} is hiring two hundred people to build it. The notice asks for anyone willing to learn.
scene W: The works says it will train anyone from the town. {N} wants to make sure that means the ones nobody usually hires.
scene U: {N} has read about the finding twice and still wants to know exactly how it works.
scene B: Two hundred jobs, and the first in will be the foremen in five years. {N} means to be among the first.
scene R: New machines, a new trade, and nobody an expert yet. {N} wants to get both hands on it.
scene G: {Ns} family worked at the old works for three generations before it closed. Now it opens again.
- W | help run the free training evenings, so anyone in town can apply | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: learn.W | chance: 72
- U | go to the lab's public talk and ask how the finding really works | v: self-direction | sphere: learn.U | chance: 80
- B | apply on the first morning, and ask what it takes to run a line | v: achievement | sphere: learn.B | chance: 70
- R | sign up for the works' training, and learn the new machines by building them | v: stimulation | mark: learned a skill | sphere: learn.R | chance: 74
- G | take the job the family would have taken, and bring a cousin along | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: learn.G | chance: 67
- BG | join the team that studies every early fault on the new line | v: security | sphere: learn.BG | chance: 62
- RG | teach the new hands on the floor the way you learned, beside them | act: teach the new hands on the floor the way they learned, beside them | v: benevolence | sphere: learn.RG | chance: 70
- UR | build a small test model at home from the published plans, and show it off | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: learn.UR | chance: 48
- WB | give to the works' training fund, so the town's young get places first | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | pushes: place | sphere: learn.WB | chance: 64
- WU | help the college write a fair entry test for the training places | v: universalism | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 58
works: {N} has a place at the works by spring, and a trade that will last.
works: The town has work again, and {N} is part of the reason.
fails: Most of the two hundred jobs go to people from outside, and {N} is not among them.
fails: The new line is slow to start, and the first year is short shifts and worry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- censors_close (pairs D6b)

