- UB | borrow the pulled books from the archivist, and lend them only to those you trust | act: borrow the pulled books from the archivist, and lend them only to those they trust | v: self-direction, security | lever: subvert | sphere: learn.UB | chance: 56
- WG | ask the parents' committee to meet the council about the list, all together | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: institution council | sphere: learn.GW | chance: 50
- WU | ask the school board to set out a fair, open rule for how books are judged | v: universalism | lever: voice | pushes: institution school | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 42
works: Within a year the books are back on the shelf, and {mentor} teaches as before.
works: {N} reads what {N} wanted to read, and learns who can be trusted with it.
fails: {mentor} is let go at the end of term, and the school is never quite the same.
