# ---------------------------------------------------------------- learned_leave (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event learned_leave, selector members, share .6
== half the class takes jobs abroad
tier: life event
sphere: learn
sphere_event: learned_leave
stages: young_adult
age: 20-30
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 3-10
times: World event: learned_leave (sphere learn). Selector members: a graduating class in a town with closed posts or low pay, where half take jobs abroad; about 6 in 10 of the class either weigh an offer of their own or lose a close friend to it (share .6, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it (estimate)
likelier: low pay or few posts at home, a degree that sells abroad, friends already gone
rarer: good posts at home, a family business waiting, a partner settled in town
tone: trouble
life: friends, work, family
horizon: years
roles: friend, parent, sibling
earth: half your graduating class takes jobs abroad, and their parents follow their lives on video calls
scene: Half of {Ns} graduating class has taken jobs abroad, {friend} among them, and the farewell parties run all summer. {N} has an offer too, and {parent} has already learned to make video calls, just in case.
scene W: Someone has to stay and teach, nurse and build here. {N} has always thought so.
scene U: The labs abroad have the equipment {N} trained for. Here there is one machine, and it is broken.
scene B: The pay abroad is three times what {N} would earn at home. The road out looks like the only road up.
